{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Map v3 is accepted and all registered work is disposed: three confirmed in-scope violations plus one reviewed bounded no-violation, with pending_work and review_issues empty. New obligation capacity is exhausted, so this step spends the remaining authorized source work resolving two boundaries recorded against confirmed findings, and it does so without inventing a Unit. Submission is a feedback-only research product (no map, so no new map version). First resolution: the installSnapshot watermark mismatch measured by check 58ebdb2f92184614b01ecfab56fe2bc9 is specific to the log-clearing branch. installSnapshot either calls removeOldLogs for a MonotonicLogStore or compactLogs(req.LastLogIndex) otherwise, and compactLogsWithTrailing only deletes [FirstIndex, min(snapIdx, lastLogIdx-trailing)] using the watermark itself as lastLogIdx, so the non-monotonic branch never removes an entry above the watermark and the watermark still names a retained entry; the mismatch requires removeOldLogs, which clears the store outright. Second resolution: the follow-on of the confirmed snapshot-trigger underflow is redundant snapshot churn. runSnapshots calls takeSnapshot whenever shouldSnapshot is true, and in the state that triggers the underflow the FSM goroutine's lastIndex is the restored snapshot index, so takeSnapshot proceeds to create and persist a full FSM snapshot at that same index every interval, re-running setLastSnapshot and compactLogs, and it repeats while the log store's last index stays below the snapshot index and stops once logs grow past it by SnapshotThreshold. Feedback cites F-log-watermark, F-snapshot, the two claims and their executed artifacts plus the compaction and snaphotter source ranges, and states explicitly that both answers are reading-based rather than new execution evidence. The remaining list keeps what this reading does